        ":question/id": "13151117-2915-58a7-8af2-4dc4a9478503",
        ":question/problem": "If $f(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x+5),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "This question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x+5).$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=2x,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x+5).\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(2x)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x+5))+({x}^{2})(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x+5)) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x+5)+6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
